> 7) You have some attributes of your character that are displayed when
> you die: You were stealthy, you were a werejackal, you were fast, etc.
> Is there a way to see these during the game? I noticed my monk became
> stealthy (not sure what it does) when he reached level 5 for example.
> So, I guess you gain these attributes though I don't know according
> to what.

No. Like identifying items, this is information the game hides from you.
Every time you gain an attibute like this, you do get a (slightly
cryptic) message, for example: "You feel full of hot air", or "You feel
jumpy". These message appear especially when you eat certain corpses,
but there's only a small chance with low level monster corpses.

> 8) I don't know some of the miscellaneous commands in the
> game do or how/why I should use them. Among these are: #invoke,
> #offer, #rub, #sit, #wipe.

I mentioned offering before. Invoking may be used with some artifacts,
rubbing and sitting will be obvious when you discover the items or
dungeon features that require them. Wiping your face is done with a
towel, which you may find.

For more information on commands, see the Guidebook file that came with
your game, or use the in-game help (?-command).

> 9) I don't know some of the miscellaneous items in the game do or
> how/why I should use them. Among these are: magic marker, towel (wipe
> but what), stethescope, looking glass. There are some others but
> that's all I can think of now.

Wipe your face when something has been thrown into it. Use a magic
marker to write on blank scrolls or spellbooks, a stethoscope does what
it does in real life (be creative!), and a looking glass is almost
useless, but provides some funny messages, for example when you're
playing a vampire (no, I'm not going to tell you how to become one!).

